Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0020.
VLLM_DSV41_MHC_FUSED_POST=1 (default off; needs the vllm_exl3_moe plugin): at each sublayer boundary of V4.1's
overlapped mHC path (patch 0014's side stream), the post (mhc_post_tilelang) and the next sublayer's input collapse
with the carried pre-mix + RMSNorm (mhc_pre_big_fuse_with_norm, split "input") run as one launch, the plugin's
mhc.post_collapse (csrc/exl3_mhc.cu: token x 256-column blocks instead of one block a token). It returns
(residual, layer_input) exactly like V4.1's fused all-reduce + mHC hook (TP=4 NVLink only), so mhc_pre_delayed_overlap
then only launches the mix statistics on the side stream. The TileLang pair costs ~12 + ~9 us at a 6-token verify step
on GB10, 80 boundaries a round (LOG Oct 11 05:52). Same fp32 FMA chain and bf16 rounding points; the RMSNorm's sum
of squares is added in another order (plugin tests/test_mhc_gpu.py: 0 differing elements at 1-8 tokens).

